00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:24.670
So, I'm gonna share this here.

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:27.230
So, this is the map that
I made about 10 years ago

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:31.223
that obviously you've seen.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:35.970
I wanna start just by
answering the questions

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.160
that you pose to all of us.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.150
How did I come to live
in the place that I live?

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:44.150
So, in the late 1960s, my dad
lived at 7,800 South Saginaw

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:49.260
which is down here on the map.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:54.100
And then in 1970, he was
with his own folded map twin

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:55.610
and moved up to the Northern Suburbs

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.910
which is where I was born.

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:01.260
And the stories that I hear
from him about why that happened

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:04.210
was, the neighborhood was changing

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:07.470
and the South side was mixed

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:09.040
when he would move there in the sixties

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.570
and was becoming much less mixed.

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:12.933
Obviously, it's now not mixed at all.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:18.770
And he wanted to have a home
that he could stay in forever,

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:24.633
have kids, et cetera and
that's my story of Chicago.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:27.420
And then the weirdest map came from,

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:28.780
I thought also was kind of speaking

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:31.233
to some of what you're
you're talking about.

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:35.140
Actually, I heard from a school teacher

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:37.520
in the suburbs of Chicago

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:40.270
and he had done a
project with some of his,

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:44.520
I think seventh graders
trying to understand Chicago

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:47.770
and the way he had done that
as to try to make some maps,

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:49.100
trying to understand exactly the things

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:49.933
you were talking about.

00:19:49.933 --> 00:19:51.270
Where are their stores?

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.450
Where are the jobs?

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:54.747
How long does it take
people to get to work?

00:19:54.747 --> 00:19:57.430
And so, they had found
all these statistics.

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:59.780
Some from the census, some from the city

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:01.350
about the kinds of things
you're talking about

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:03.290
and they'd made a bunch of maps of them.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:05.700
And the one map that just wasn't working

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:06.670
was the map of race.

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:07.750
They just couldn't make a map

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.870
that they could really make much sense of.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.660
And all the maps that
they had been making,

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:14.150
all the maps that I had seen myself

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:16.070
looked like this one in the bottom left

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:19.950
where you shaded every
neighborhood a solid color

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:23.020
and it certainly showed you
places like the South side

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:25.570
and the West side but it
didn't really give you a sense

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:28.133
of how stark the segregation really was.

00:20:28.133 --> 00:20:29.530
- Yes.
- And so the map

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:32.280
that you see here that
with all the little dots

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:35.830
is what I came up with in my conversations

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.830
with this middle school teacher as a way

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.820
to getting kids in the
suburbs to understand

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:44.320
just how stark the divisions were

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:49.320
and just how removed their own lives were

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.230
from the vast majority of
people that live in the city.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:57.030
And it's really great for
me to see you making use

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:59.872
of the same map in your project.

00:20:59.872 --> 00:21:03.320
- So, have you made the map,
'cause I was searching for it.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:06.350
I was like, "Oh my gosh, does this exist?"

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:09.448
And lo and behold, I found your map.

00:21:09.448 --> 00:21:10.440
(chuckles)

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:11.273
- That's great.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:14.730
