to people in the schools,

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:31.130
they want to put this in
some exhibition somewhere,

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:33.980
and it's about doing work on
the city of Chicago exactly.

00:21:35.175 --> 00:21:36.008
And the other thing-
- You and I

00:21:36.008 --> 00:21:39.144
definitely have to link up and partner.

00:21:39.144 --> 00:21:40.020
(both laugh)

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.860
- Yeah, it'd be great.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:44.680
And then, there's this
map that I actually made

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:45.980
when I moved to New Haven.

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:48.690
And it was a way of just
trying to understand

00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:49.523
what was going on

00:21:49.523 --> 00:21:52.580
in the place that I was
going to be living in,

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:55.840
and how did I come to
live in that place I live?

00:21:55.840 --> 00:22:00.320
I live in this mostly
but not all pink area

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:01.883
right around here in East Rock.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:08.010
And a lot of it was actually
not so much talking to people

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:10.420
and getting nudged by realtors
and that kind of stuff.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.860
It was looking up where
the restaurants were,

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:14.700
where the cafes were,

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:17.860
where could I live close to work and walk

00:22:18.794 --> 00:22:20.145
and those kinds of things.

00:22:20.145 --> 00:22:21.796
(indistinct chatter)

00:22:21.796 --> 00:22:23.013
- I lived in the same neighborhood

00:22:23.013 --> 00:22:26.905
and for me, the main criterion
was, can I walk to work?

00:22:26.905 --> 00:22:30.103
- Yeah, yeah and can I walk to a cafe?

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:34.790
I used like Thai food,
can I find Thai food?

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:36.080
I really like Thai food.

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:38.842
And so it was those questions that led me

00:22:38.842 --> 00:22:43.070
to really confront the
segregation in New Haven

00:22:43.070 --> 00:22:45.220
because the kinds of things
that I thought were important

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:47.340
in my life were the things that existed

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:49.350
in the predominantly white neighborhoods

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:51.130
instead of the other neighborhoods.

00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:51.963
- Wow.

00:22:51.963 --> 00:22:54.207
- Mostly it's saying thank
you Tonika for that project,

00:22:54.207 --> 00:22:55.940
really great.

00:22:55.940 --> 00:22:58.580
And yeah, I'm really glad

00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:01.297
to be able to share that far and wide now.

00:23:01.297 --> 00:23:02.900
- Yeah, now this is amazing

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:07.707
and I definitely would
love to partner with you

